{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "lem:full-critical-covariance",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For the full scores from def:full-score-covariance, including the harmonic translation score and the covariance between the leading and generated-target responses within each control cell, \\(\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal F_s}\\lVert\\Sigma_{h_n}(P)-V(P)\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}}\\to0\\), where \\(V(P)=\\operatorname{diag}(V_1,\\ldots,V_J)\\), \\(V_j=w_j\\sqrt{\\det H(y_j)}H(y_j)/(4\\pi f_{T1}(y_j))\\), and \\(w_j=\\alpha(y_j)(\\rho_{C0}^{-1}+\\rho_{C1}^{-1})+\\rho_{T0}^{-1}+\\rho_{T1}^{-1}\\). The normalized harmonic variance and every Green--harmonic cross-covariance vanish by the uniform \\(L^2\\) bound in thm:nested-derivative.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(P\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal F_s\\)",
      "\\(\\Sigma_h(P)\\)",
      "\\(h_n\\)",
      "\\(V(P)\\)",
      "\\(J\\)",
      "\\(j\\)",
      "\\(H\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal Y_J\\)",
      "\\(f_g\\)",
      "\\(\\alpha\\)",
      "\\(\\rho_g\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal H_P\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:four-sample-design",
      "ass:cell-ratios",
      "ass:fixed-separated-grid",
      "ass:outer-ellipticity",
      "ass:lift-regularity",
      "ass:polynomial-bandwidth",
      "lem:uniform-critical-estimates",
      "def:nested-derivative",
      "def:full-score-covariance",
      "thm:nested-derivative",
      "ass:density-positivity"
    ],
    "justification": "The corrected derivative now proves bounded harmonic variance and fixes the algebraic four-cell logarithmic coefficient.",
    "gap": "Uniform replacement of transformed, moving-pole scores by their frozen local responses remains open.",
    "consumer": "The displayed matrix remains a candidate covariance until that singular score comparison closes.",
    "proof_tex": "By lem:uniform-critical-estimates, for every cell and grid point the exact score is its mollified frozen \\(1/r\\) Green field plus an \\(L^2(P_g)\\)-bounded remainder.  Therefore the remainder variance divided by \\(L_n\\) is \\(O(L_n^{-1})\\), and its cross-covariance with the leading score divided by \\(L_n\\) is \\(O(L_n^{-1/2})\\), uniformly by Cauchy--Schwarz.  This applies in particular to the complete harmonic term from thm:nested-derivative and to the order-minus-two generated-target term.\n\nFix \\(y_j\\), put \\(B_j=B(y_j)\\), and use the frozen fundamental solution\n\\[\n \\Gamma_j(z)=-\\frac{1}{2\\pi\\sqrt{\\det B_j}}\n \\log|B_j^{-1/2}z|.\n\\tag{1}\n\\]\nWith \\(z=B_j^{1/2}r\\omega\\), \\(\\omega\\in\\mathbb S^1\\), and\n\\(\\int_{\\mathbb S^1}\\omega\\omega^{\\mathsf T}d\\omega=\\pi I_2\\), direct integration gives\n\\[\n \\int_{h<|z|<r_0}\\nabla\\Gamma_j(z)\\nabla\\Gamma_j(z)^{\\mathsf T}dz\n =\\frac{B_j^{-1}}{4\\pi\\sqrt{\\det B_j}}\\log(1/h)+O(1).\n\\tag{2}\n\\]\nThe inner and outer boundaries may be replaced by uniformly nondegenerate ellipses because this changes only the \\(O(1)\\) term.  Lem:uniform-critical-estimates proves that convolution by \\(K_h^{\\mathrm{per}}\\), the variable coefficient, and the nonlinear coordinate pullback also alter (2) by \\(o(\\log(1/h))\\), uniformly.\n\nWe compute the four local intensities without discarding within-cell cross terms.  The mass identities are\n\\[\n f_{C1}(T(y))\\det H(y)=f_{C0}(R_0(y))\\det D(y),\n \\qquad f_{T0}(R_0(y))\\det D(y)=f_{T1}(y).\n\\tag{3}\n\\]\nFor either control cell, the squared leading multiplier is \\(\\alpha(y_j)^2\\), while the pullback intensity before that multiplication is\n\\(f_{C0}(R_0(y_j))\\det D(y_j)=f_{T1}(y_j)/\\alpha(y_j)\\).  Hence each control cell has local intensity \\(\\alpha(y_j)f_{T1}(y_j)\\).  Each treated cell has local intensity \\(f_{T1}(y_j)\\).  The two appearances of a control noise in def:nested-derivative were combined before squaring; their order-minus-two and harmonic parts are in the bounded remainder, so their cross-products with the leading part are exactly among the vanishing terms above.  Independence in ass:four-sample-design removes cross-cell, but not within-cell, covariances.  It follows from (2)--(3) and ass:cell-ratios that the \\((j,j)\\) block tends to\n\\[\n f_{T1}(y_j)w_j\\frac{B_j^{-1}}{4\\pi\\sqrt{\\det B_j}},\n \\quad\n w_j=\\alpha(y_j)(\\rho_{C0}^{-1}+\\rho_{C1}^{-1})\n      +\\rho_{T0}^{-1}+\\rho_{T1}^{-1}.\n\\tag{4}\n\\]\nSince \\(B_j=f_{T1}(y_j)H(y_j)^{-1}\\),\n\\[\n f_{T1}(y_j)w_j\\frac{B_j^{-1}}{4\\pi\\sqrt{\\det B_j}}\n =\\frac{w_j\\sqrt{\\det H(y_j)}H(y_j)}{4\\pi f_{T1}(y_j)}=V_j.\n\\tag{5}\n\\]\nIf \\(j\\neq k\\), ass:fixed-separated-grid and invertibility of the pullbacks keep the two poles a fixed positive distance apart.  Near either pole the other singular field is bounded, so their product is locally integrable; the cross-block covariance is therefore \\(O(1)/L_n=o(1)\\).  Equations (4)--(5), summed over the four independent cells, prove\n\\(\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal F_s}\\lVert\\Sigma_{h_n}(P)-V(P)\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}}\\to0\\).\n\nMoreover, ass:density-positivity, ass:outer-ellipticity, and\n\\(1\\leq\\rho_g\\leq\\bar\\rho\\) give\n\\[\n \\lambda_{\\min}(V_j)\n \\geq\\frac{\\lambda^2}{4\\pi C\\bar\\rho}>0,\n\\tag{6}\n\\]\nso the asserted positive definiteness is uniform.",
